CSharpAuthor 2.0 migration patch — DependencyModules
Generated 2026-08-21 by `git diff` in a clone of github.com/ipjohnson/DependencyModules
at 642bac3 (Release 1.0.0, #39), and verified with `git apply --check`
against a pristine clone of the same commit.

Measured against CSharpAuthor `feature/v2` at 4c7dc35.

Measured, 8 test assemblies, both TFMs:
  1.1.1010 baseline   1,812 passed / 0 failed
  2.0 unpatched         770 passed / 704 failed, and only 4 assemblies —
                        SutProject fails to build, so SutProject.Tests and
                        SutProject.NUnitTests never run at all
  2.0 with this patch 1,792 passed /  20 failed, every one a snapshot pin:
                        9 ModuleGenerationSnapshotTests + PublicApiTests.SourceGeneratorApi,
                        each on net8.0 and net10.0. Justified one by one in
                        docs/migration-v1-v2.md section 9.6. No snapshot was re-baselined;
                        UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS was unset for every run.

Every hunk was verified necessary by reverting it alone.

NOTE ON THE VERSION LINE. The <PackageReference> bump to 2.0.0 is included because
it is part of the migration, but CSharpAuthor 2.0.0 is not published yet, so a
`dotnet restore` after applying this will fail with NU1102. To exercise the patch
today, apply it, put the version line back, and point the build at a 2.0 checkout —
see docs/migration-v1-v2.md section 9.2. Every measurement quoted above was taken
that way, with the wiring proved on each run.

diff --git a/src/DependencyModules.SourceGenerator.Impl/DecoratorFileWriter.cs b/src/DependencyModules.SourceGenerator.Impl/DecoratorFileWriter.cs
